# Allow-list, not deny-list.
#
# A deny-list that misses one directory ships it to the daemon on every build, and
# two directories here make that unacceptable rather than merely slow:
#
#   References/  ~1.4 GB of read-only prototype and vendor schema material.
#   .claude/     plaintext dev secrets (DB password, JWT secret, encryption key).
#
# Anything in the build context can end up in an image layer, and a later `RUN rm`
# does not remove it from the layer — it would ship to the registry. So: deny
# everything, then name what a build actually needs.

*

# --- what the builds need ---
!src/
!apps/
!tests/
!RadiologyPlus.sln
!global.json
!Directory.Build.props

# --- re-exclude noise inside the allowed trees (last match wins) ---
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.user

# Never let host-local config or secrets into a layer. appsettings.json ships
# (it carries log levels and non-secret defaults); the Development/Local overrides
# do not exist in git but may exist on disk.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# .git is excluded by the `*` above. Pass the commit in explicitly instead:
#   docker build --build-arg GIT_SHA=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD) ...
